This was probably my 70th attempt at a pacifist ascension.  Last month,
I posted a YAAP for an almost pacifist healer (pacifism lasted until turn
65k when I found out my Archon was too low-level to fight the lively WoY,
lost my focus, and ran into a lichen).  I learned much from that game and
applied lessons learnt on a public nethack server (nethack.alt.org).
On my 8th game this was the final result:

Pmc the Enchantress       St:18 Dx:15 Co:16 In:21 Wi:19 Ch:13  Chaotic S:12700
Astral Plane $:0  HP:290(297) Pw:192(192) AC:-41 Xp:14/80000 T:60159

My starting stats:
St:10 Dx:15 Co:15 In:17 Wi:8 Ch:10 HP:11(11) Pw:8(8) AC:9

I began with a spellbook of protection and a ring of poison resistance.
With the ring of poison resistance I was able to eat pretty much anything.
I waited until I had enough nutrition and food stored before I prayed the
first time hunger beset my character.  This set my alignment to 1 for
future food prayers.

My pet cat, Cauchy, liberated a cloak of invisibility from a kobold on
dungeon level 5. I took off my [oMR and enjoyed dancing around low-level
monsters.

Cauchy hit a level teleport trap on Dlvl:6. While petless for only
1200 turns, I found the oracle on Dlvl:7 but my way was blocked by
a gas spore in a hallway. Not wanting to risk a projectile being thrown,
I retreated up the stairs and found a general store on Dlvl:2 where I
sold most of my belongings ($1247).

With heavy pockets I went back to the oracle level, took the inevitable
risk, pushed back the gas spore, a couple of manes, and a homunculus with
glyphs written in dust.

HP:26(26) Pw:30(30) AC:9 Xp:3/41 T:2143

I found Cauchy two levels below the Oracle dangerously close
to a white unicorn, we quickly retreated up the stairs.  As we
fled upward I found more armor and decided to stop using the
protection spell in lieu of a solid AC of 1 (+2 chain mail,
+0 orcish helm, +0 cloak of invis).

I entered the mines (Dlvl:2) with my large cat Cauchy and found a
bones file haunted by two previous occupants.  I received a second
large cat as a pet (named Gluino) and a magic marker.  I explored
the right half of the level and found what the previous adventurers
did not: an uncursed Wand of Wishing (0:1). (Turn 4766).

On GM:6 I found the mine town and a co-aligned altar.  I obtained three
points of protection (AC:-2), recharged the WoW, and received +3 SDSM.
AC: -8 -> ([oMR, SDSM, iron skull cap, low boots) - only one watchman had
gloves and they were cursed. The tool shop contained a magic whistle,
a leash, a magic marker, and an oilskin sack.

I decided to venture further down the mines, found a +2 hard hat (AC:-11),
and saw this message on GM-8: "The dwarf deliberately jumps onto a polymorph
trap!".  My cats took down the raven in no time.  After a few whistles,
Gluino became a Demilich.  A floating eye paralyzed Cauchy then jumped
onto the trap becoming a Yeti.  Both pets were useless in my fight against
the Yeti; dusty elbereth bought me some time to revitalize Cauchy and
turn him into a Dwarf King.  Then *another* floating eye jumped onto the
trap becoming a blue dragon.  Needless to say the SDSM saved my life.
My team and I found the downstairs (right next to the poly-trap and
the upstairs) and explored the rest of the mines (Bottom was GM:10).

Returning to mine town, Gluino, the Master Lich, started taking down
the shopkeepers -> Base AC:1.  After donations, I explored the
rest of the upper levels of the mines and found a blessed permanent light
source.  In the course of explorations of the mines I received
poison resistance, telepathy, and permanent invisibility.

I continued exploration of the DoD.  A troll with a wand of death killed
Cauchy the Dwarf King on dungeon level 17.  Another troll came along
to back up his death wielding friend.  I was taking heavy damage (still
having a max HP of 26) so I retreated a level and made my third
wish for +3 speed boots -> AC:-20.  With the speed boots and invisibility
I was able to keep my distance from the trolls and let Gluino finish
them off.

I lost Gluino on dungeon level 21 to level-teleport trap and found him
still tame on dungeon level 11.  Where I found Gluino, I also found a
polymorph trap and started making new pets that did not have the staying
power of my arch-lich: a Vampire, a gargoyle, an ice devil, and
a demon whose make and model I forget.

With these secondary pets, I started giving burnt offerings to my deity.
After awhile I quaffed a potion of gain level, ate a wraith corpse, had
a small alchemy session, and enchanted my armor to +4:

St:18 Dx:15 Co:16 In:17 Wi:12 Ch:10
HP:81 Pw:58 AC:-32 Xp:5

For some reason, my demon became a guardian naga (maybe there
was an unfound poly-trap or it got hit by a potion of polymorph).  Either
way the guardian naga was a powerful compliment to my arch-lich (paralyzing
monsters and killing off the cold resistant).

Around turn 30k I decided to do sokoban and mainly just picked up rings
and wands I had already identified.

I dug past Medusa and floated around to the back entrance of the castle.
I lost my guardian naga eventually in the ensuing fight but my arch-lich
prevailed.  The castle wand was at (0:1) and I kept it for backup.

With an Hawaiian shirt found in the castle armory and more protection,
I reached AC:-37. I received Stealth from my deity and performed another
round of alchemy: HP:188 Xp:5.

At this point, I genocided L (losing my faithful pet arch-lich without
any penalties -- is this a feature?).  I used my 4th wish on a blessed
figurine of an Archon.  The Archon, Gluino, was created with Sunsword.
He killed off Medusa and we collected wraith corpses in the VotD:

HP:223 Pw:142 AC:-37 Xp:10 T:43235

Entering a Gehennom, I forgot to tell Asmodeus that I had gold in my
oilskin sack.  I left him on his level, bribed Baalzebub, and Juiblex
got godsmacked by a /oDigging.

HP:230 Pw:150 AC:-38 Xp:11 T:45351

I left Gehennom at Dlvl: 36 where Orcus was at and returned to minetown
to continue casting 'create monster'.  My 5th and last wish on my first
WoW was for a cursed magic marker.  I reverse-genocided Wraiths
to reach Xp:14 and white unicorns to enter the Quest.

HP:244 Pw:192 AC:-38 Xp:14 T:48162

The Dark One was no problem for Gluino -- I continued sacrificing
monsters and reached a base armour class of -4.

HP:249 Pw:192 AC:-41 Xp:14

At turn 50k my pet and I level-telported past Orcus and killed Vlad (Dlvl:37).
We continued to map the mazes and the archon hit a level-teleport trap
on Dlvl:41 on turn 51k.  I found him eventually on Dlvl:6 (peaceful).  I left
him there.

At this point, petless, I decided to lure Asmodeus to Vlad's Tower so
he would not be a problem for me as I made the marathon dash to the Endgame.
With an AC of -41 and Magicbane to liberally engrave Elbereth he was just
an annoyance.  He gated in Geryon for help, but both were left abandoned in
Vlad's Tower.

My 6th wish was for a new pet Archon named Photino created with Demonbane.
I let Photino naturally level-up, gave him 3 potions of gain level, enchanted
his new long sword, Frost Brand, to +7 (a gift from my deity with a starting
bonus of +3), a spare "oLS, unicorn horn, +6 elven leather helm, +2 leather
gloves, and +0 iron shoes:

Status for Photino: XP:32 HP:256 AC:-20

I used my 7th wish for a blessed stethoscope (the only useful items I got
from polypiling was a magic marker and a ring of free action).

At this point I felt Photino was ready to fight the Wizard of Yendor.  First
we took out Orcus (he only fire one round).  The WoY went down in two rounds.

We continued onto to Moloch's Sanctum.  With stealth the zoo of undead were
picked off one-by one.  The priests did not last long.  And the high priest
was of no consequence.

On our way back up with the Amulet we got knocked back from the upstairs
several times:
45->46, 45->46, 45->46, 43->44, 36->37, 35->35, 35->35, 32->33, 30->31, and
30->31.

At level 27 we reached the VotD and at level 11 I reached my stash to
double check my inventory.  Photino and I were ready for the final ascent.

Status of Photino: XP:34 HP:272 AC:-20 (I found 2 potions of gain level
in the WoY's zoo and 1 potion of gain level in the Sanctum's zoo).

The Plane of Earth was no problem, the WoY went down in two rounds again.
The Plane of Air was equally easy with many wands of slow monster, wands
of opening, and wands of teleportation.  (I was only engulfed once by an
energy vortex and once by an Earth Elemental).
On the Plane of Fire I decided to genocide vortices.
On the Astral Plane, I put on my "oLS for the first time (it was totally
unnecessary), and I chose the left path, which was correct.  Death
was easily dispatched by Photino (2 round KO).

